{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Miriam spoke.</b> She was the one who spoke, and therefore she was punished; and Aaron either agreed or was silent. Yet we find that he too was punished, as it says ״ויחר אף ה' בם״ — and the anger of YHWH burned against them — including them both in the wrath. And every place where חרון אף (wrath) is said of HaShem, it leaves an impression; but in the case of Miriam, who initiated the evil speech, the punishment became public, whereas in Aaron's case it was not made public, for his honor." "<b>Concerning the Cushite woman.</b> This is Zipporah, who is a Midianite; and Midianites are Ishmaelites, and they dwell in tents, as it is written (Habakkuk 3:7–8): ״ירגזו יריעות ארץ מדין״. And there is no difference between them and a black man (כושי) because of the intensity of the sun's heat. And the meaning of ״אשה כושית לקח״ is the matter of the words that Miriam spoke: they thought that Moses refrained from being with Zipporah only because she was not beautiful. And Onkelos, who translated אתתא שפירתא, used a circumlocution of honor, just as they call a blind person סגי נהור (one who has abundant light). And therefore it says ״והאיש משה ענו מאד״ — and the man Moses was very humble — for Scripture testifies to his humility, that he did not notice whether she was beautiful or not, in the same manner mentioned concerning Abraham our father." "<b>And Rashi</b>, of blessed memory, explained: ״אשה כושית״ — a beautiful woman; and on account of her beauty she is called כושית, like a person who calls his beautiful daughter כושית so that the evil eye should not gain dominion over her. And the sense of ״על אודות האשה הכושית״ is: concerning his divorcing her — for ״אשה כושית לקח״ — he had taken a Cushite woman — and now he divorced her. And thus כושית in gematria is יפת מראה."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:31:49.303238316Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}